{
    "background_story": "Callahan was a warbler of the Dendroica species, known for his vibrant yellow plumage and distinctive song. He spent his summers flitting through the dense forests of North America, feasting on insects and berries. But Callahan's true passion was music. Every morning, he would perch on a branch high above the forest floor and sing his heart out, filling the air with a sweet, melodic trill. His song was so enchanting that it attracted a flock of fellow warblers, who would gather around him to sing in harmony. As the seasons changed, Callahan would migrate to the warmer climates of Central America, but his love of music remained constant. He became a legend among the bird community, known as the 'Songmaster of the Dendroica'. His melodies brought joy to all who heard them, and his legacy lived on long after he was gone.",
